## Summary

Audited main at 7df5dffe7b94a906f4f2a3f6ce690828b1e51f8e for reachable security issues against the documented trust model. Found and reproduced #208: a Home-only admin could bind another app's managers group as an app/widget/link audience, then add/remove its members or rules and take over its events or lists. The original ordinary API batch returned HTTP 200 and made Rowan Ashdown a Fall Picnic manager.

Fixed the common home_audience policy predicate, so Home-specific membership/rule grants apply only to unmanaged top-level plain groups without a slug, excluding groups that manage anything, serve as app admins, or hold hidden-list membership. This preserves normal dedicated Home audiences while refusing authority gained solely by selecting a foreign group as an audience. Added API regressions for app/widget/link bindings, all four membership/rule edits, unmanaged managers and unrelated child groups; updated docs/home/data.md. Home admins must use dedicated Viewers groups or the foreign group's existing management permissions to change its membership or rules.

Review completed, then main merged automatically using git merge --no-ff --no-commit main, without conflicts or manual resolution. On the merged tree the full internal/db suite passed in 17.6 seconds, auth/MCP/app/imagesearch/mail tests and the incoming geocode tests passed under timeout 30, and go vet ./... and git diff --check passed. The merge was left uncommitted for byre to conclude as requested.

Left deliberately public share previews, documented API bearer-token capabilities, and trusted system/super-admin access unchanged. No additional demonstrated vulnerability established in other inspected boundaries. No deployment performed. Security issue: https://github.com/heliosian/heliosian/issues/208.

